# Data Fetching & API Layer

Prefer the core hooks over ad-hoc `useEffect` + axios (see [client/src/hooks/README.md](client/src/hooks/README.md)):

- `useApiQuery` for GET (auto-fetch, returns `{ data, loading, error, refetch }`)
- `useApiMutation` for POST/PUT/DELETE (toasts on success/error)

## API Layer

Add request methods to the relevant `*Api.js` object using `API_ENDPOINTS`, and export it from [client/src/api/index.js](client/src/api/index.js). Avoid hardcoded paths.

```js
// GOOD - in blogApi.js
getAll: async () => axios.get(API_ENDPOINTS.BLOGS_ALL)

// AVOID - hardcoded path in a hook
axios.post('/api/blog/add', formData)
```

## Hooks

The backend always returns `{ success, message?, ...payload }`. Map nested data with a fallback, and register the hook in the relevant barrel.

```js
// queries/useBlogs.js
export function useBlogs() {
  const { data, loading, error, refetch } = useApiQuery(
    () => blogApi.getAll(),
    { errorMessage: MESSAGES.ERROR_FETCH_BLOGS }
  )
  return { blogs: data?.blogs || [], loading, error, refetch }
}
```

Export new query hooks from `hooks/api/queries/index.js` and mutations from `hooks/api/mutations/index.js`.
